0000:                   *
0000:                   *   PIPEMAN
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   Pipe File Manager
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   WARNING
0000:                   *   -------
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   Opening an existing named pipe emulates IOMan's I$Close and
0000:                   *   I$Dup calls.  This file manager contains subroutines that
0000:                   *   mimic the current operation of IOMan.  Any changes to IOMan's
0000:                   *   FMEXEC, I$Close or I$Dup calls must also be made to this code.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   Device Driver Static Storage Layout
0000:                   *   -----------------------------------
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   $00-$01 V.List  Pointer in system map to pipe buffer for 1st
0000:                   *                   pipe (16 bits).
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   Pipe Buffer Data Structure
0000:                   *   --------------------------
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   $00-$01 PP.PD   Pointer to shared path descriptor
0000:                   *   $02-$03 PP.Next Pointer to next pipe buffer in system map
0000:                   *   $04-$05 PP.Prev Pointer to previous pipe buffer in system map
0000:                   *   $06-$07 PP.Rsv2 Reserved
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   $08     PP.Data Data buffer begins at this offset
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   Path Descriptor Data Structure
0000:                   *   ------------------------------
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   $00     PD.PD   Path number
0000:                   *   $01     PD.MOD  Access permissions
0000:                   *   $02     PD.CNT  Number of open images (e.g. I$DUP)
0000:                   *   $05     PD.CPR  Current process ID
0000:                   *   $06-$07 PD.RGS  Address of caller's register stack
0000:                   *   $08-$09 PD.BUF  System space pipe buffer base pointer
0000:                   *** PP.Read must have bit 4 clear; PP.Writ must be PP.Read XOR 4
0000:                   *  $0A      PD.Read No bytes -- offset only
0000:                   *   $0A     PD.RPID Process ID of reader waiting on signal
0000:                   *   $0B     PD.RCT  Number of blocked readers
0000:                   *   $0C     PD.RSIG Signal to send reader
0000:                   *   $0D     PD.REOR Read EOR character
0000:                   *  $0E      PD.Writ No bytes -- offset only
0000:                   *   $0E     PD.WPID Process ID of writer waiting on signal
0000:                   *   $0F     PD.WCT  Number of blocked writers
0000:                   *   $10     PD.WSIG Signal to send writer
0000:                   *   $11     PD.WEOR Write EOR character (dummy)
0000:                   *** End of special section
0000:                   *   $12-$13 PD.End  Pointer to end of pipe buffer
0000:                   *   $14-$15 PD.NxtI Next in pointer
0000:                   *   $16-$17 PD.NxtO Next out pointer
0000:                   *   $18     PD.RFlg "Ready" flag
0000:                   *   $19     PD.Wrtn "Written" flag
0000:                   *   $1A-$1B PD.BCnt # queue elements currently bufered
0000:                   *   $1C     PD.Own  Process ID of pipe original creator
0000:                   *   $1D     PD.Keep Non-zero if this pipe has been kept open artificially
0000:                   *   $1E-$1F PD.QSiz Max. size of queue (in elements)
0000:                   *   .
0000:                   *   .
0000:                   *   $20     PD.DTP  Device type $02 = PIPE
0000:                   *   $21     PD.ESiz Size of each queue element
0000:                   *   $22-$23 PD.ECnt Max. elements in queue
0000:                   *   $23-$3F PD.Name Pipe name (after moving PD.ECnt to PD.QSiz)
0000:                   *
0000:                   
0000:                            page  
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   Global equates
0000:                   *
0000:                            IFP1  
0000:                            use   defsfile
0000:                            use   pipe.d
0000:                            ENDC  
0000:                   
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   Local Equates
0000:                   *
0000:                   
0003:                   XVER     equ   3          ;Version
0000:                   
0000:                   *   ASCII CONTROL CHARACTERS
0000:                   
000D:                   CR       equ   $0D
0000:                   
0000:                   *   CONDITION CODES
0000:                   
0000:                   *   PIPEMAN SPECIAL OFFSETS.
0000:                   
0000:                   PM.CPR   equ   PD.RPID-PD.READ
0001:                   PM.CNT   equ   PD.RCT-PD.READ
0002:                   PM.SIG   equ   PD.RSIG-PD.READ
0003:                   PM.EOR   equ   PD.REOR-PD.READ
0000:                   
0000:                   *   IOMAN special offsets.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   This constant is IOMAN release-dependent.
0000:                   *   It is the number of bytes between the entry stack
0000:                   *   pointer and the stacked PD pointer saved by *IOMAN*.
0000:                   *   Currently, the stack looks like this:
0000:                   *
0000:                   *       A   PL
0000:                   *       9   PH  <IOMAN post-SOPEN return address>
0000:                   *       8   UL
0000:                   *       7   UH
0000:                   *       6   YL  +
0000:                   *       5   YH  <PD pointer saved by IOMAN>
0000:                   *       4   XL
0000:                   *       3   XH
0000:                   *       2   A
0000:                   *       1   PL
0000:                   * SP->  0   PH  <post OPEN/CREATE return address>
0000:                   *               <start of stack to be used by PIPEMAN>
0000:                   
0005:                   IOMAGIC  equ   5          ;5 bytes to PD pointer
0000:                   
0000:                   *   Local pipe buffer equates
0000:                   
0020:                   CInit    equ   %00100000  ;Set this bit to override PD queue parameters
0000:                   
0000:                   *   Conditional assembly
0000:                   
0000:                   ANON     set   0          ;Anonymous pipes only
0001:                   NAMED    set   1          ;Anonymous and named pipes
0002:                   MSGS     set   2          ;Both types of pipes, and message queues
0001:                   WIZBANG  set   NAMED      ;What features are we providing?
0000:                   
0000:                   NODIR    set   0          ;Don't allow DIR on pipe devices
0001:                   YESDIR   set   1          ;Allow DIR on pipe devices
0001:                   PIPEDIR  set   YESDIR     ;Does DIR work on pipes?
0000:                   
0000:                   SLOWPD   set   0          ;Slow PD location algorithm
0001:                   QUICKPD  set   1          ;Fast PD location algorithm
0001:                   PDALGO   set   QUICKPD    ;How to convert PD to system path #
0000:                   
0000:                   RECKLES  set   0          ;Don't check for certain errors
0001:                   CAREFUL  set   1          ;Check for certain errors
0001:                   CAUTION  set   CAREFUL
0000:                   
